  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MMR005N Myanmar Earthquake ACJR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project combines life-saving MPCA with targeted protection services to address urgent and diverse needs of 8720 affected IDPs and host communities in Mandalay. CARE and LCM will implement MPC+Protection in Aung Myay Thar Zan and Mahar Aung Myay,  and respectively CARE and DO in Pyi Gyi Tagon, ensuring local ownership, gender expertise, and community trust. 

MPCA: Drawing on findings from the RNA/RMA, MPC was identified as the most appropriate and effective modality, enabling HH to meet essential needs (food, WASH, shelter/NFIs) through market-based solutions. Based on the recent CWG meeting of 31/3, 1 round of gender-sensitive MPCA will be delivered to 1,600 HH (6,720 individuals, covering 1 month of basic needs), with values adapted to HH size (average 4.2) in line with national CWG, and Nov 2024 MEB. Priority will be given to PwDs, pregnant and lactating women, female-headed HH, and those composed solely of elderly and children.

Protection: tailored cluster-standard dignity kits (DK) will be provided to 2,000 disaster-affected women and girls, accompanied by awareness-raising and dissemination of referral pathways delivered in community-based mobile friendly spaces. Awareness sessions on protection, PSEA, and safe use of cash will be ensure safe, dignified, and informed access to assistance.

Activities are aligned with the CHS, and DRA guidelines. The programme builds on lessons from the Myanmar JR &#x2018;23&amp;&#x2019;24 and ensures strong coordination with all submitting DRA partners, through target alignment, joint PDMs and sharing of BNFs-list/criteria. Duplication will be avoided with Tearfund, ZOA &amp; Oxfam operating in the same large townships with high needs, and MPC harmonization with Cordaid, ZOA, Tearfund, Plan, Oxfam and WV. Protection referrals will be coordinated with all. Coordination will be ensured with AHCT, Area ICCG, OCHA, and relevant clusters.</narrative>
  </description>
